<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:03:53Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Zelenskyy visits Norway amid Trump White House tensions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7aaca452498dfc81b0eeae2b6e309851bc0f5d0c2219c6344f4b198effd8bfac</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:03:29Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T19:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/zelenskyy-visits-norway-amid-trump-white-house-tensions/a-79717354--f26d4c094394.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/zelenskyy-visits-norway-amid-trump-white-house-tensions/a-79717354?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Zelenskyy met with Norwegian and Finnish leaders in Oslo and held talks with Trump envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner. Trump is pressuring Zelenskyy to "make a deal" with Russia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria records its first Ebola case, in capital Abuja</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:41a924a3530342fad3bcc6ddbb6148ab040bc00137140ecf33f2fcdd8af632f1</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:03:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T19:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-records-its-first-ebola-case-in-capital-abuja/a-79717377--c6985b1c776f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-records-its-first-ebola-case-in-capital-abuja/a-79717377?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nigeria has reported its first known case of Ebola during Africa's latest outbreak originating in the DRC. Health Minister Muhammad Ali Pate said the patient was a woman who had recently flown to Abuja from Uganda.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Lebanon faces uncertainty as UNIFIL mandate nears end</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:35fb078ebe9ddaeb59b1f641f3995fc34c9bb1774e1a27cf54a088137987a4c2</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:03:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T18:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/lebanon-faces-uncertainty-as-unifil-mandate-nears-end/a-79714491--a12453a4b744.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/lebanon-faces-uncertainty-as-unifil-mandate-nears-end/a-79714491?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As UN peacekeeping forces prepare to withdraw from Lebanon, Israel remains present and Hezbollah is still armed. A new EU support mission aims to strengthen Lebanon's army, but will not replace UN peacekeepers.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Sudan drone strike kills around 150 in Abyei market</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:50e537b6b8e89dd6183123d07932979e8af4d8fccbf59a465357a3b68a8d585e</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:03:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T18:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/sudan-drone-strike-kills-around-150-in-abyei-market/a-79716587--6d5e17c39f6a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/sudan-drone-strike-kills-around-150-in-abyei-market/a-79716587?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A drone strike hit a market in the Abyei border region disputed by Sudan and South Sudan and killed dozens. The drone caused a large fire when it hit a fuel depot. South Sudanese officials blamed Sudan's military.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>North Korean workers treated as 'slaves' at Russian drone factory, says new report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ef9309c97e160d17723f00857b017349de5a4338f2ec639e7eecd624be419794</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:02:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T17:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korean-workers-treated-as-slaves-at-russian-drone-factory-says-new-report/a-79710877--a509ee21abbc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korean-workers-treated-as-slaves-at-russian-drone-factory-says-new-report/a-79710877?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new report reveals the plight of North Korean workers at a drone factory in Russia. It also raised concerns that Pyongyang could gain hands-on knowledge of advanced weapons systems through the workers it sends there.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>New EU plan for Arctic warily eyes influence of Russia, US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:012c68830a841c543fa2f0918f0d4e964d1a8eec83fd1a90746194a164e2d4dd</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:03:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T16:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/new-eu-plan-for-arctic-warily-eyes-influence-of-russia-us/a-79715219--7030ab283919.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/new-eu-plan-for-arctic-warily-eyes-influence-of-russia-us/a-79715219?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU unveiled its priorities in the Arctic as it vies with Russia, China and the US for influence. EU foreign affairs chief Kaja Kallas said drone incursions, GPS jamming and cable sabotage undermine Arctic security.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France plans 'massive' weekend police surge amid protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:070d4723647b148e30e90d02ef92e806505f5df695e2d723b8f206c3fdc6eeeb</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:03:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T15:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-plans-massive-weekend-police-surge-amid-protests/live-79707186--61242b391ca9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-plans-massive-weekend-police-surge-amid-protests/live-79707186?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">French Prime Minister Sebastien Lecornu told parliament the government would respond and reinforce police in major cities. He also accused extreme-left groups of trying to hijack what began as protests. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Hackers release AfD party emails</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e63a6a19a58c3c66b5888d0eed6dbbfcd9e10301c1d2256b20bb27bf6bdf4923</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:03:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T15:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-hackers-release-afd-party-emails/live-79709090--0adf9ddcd090.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-hackers-release-afd-party-emails/live-79709090?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's far-right AfD has launched an inquiry after the release of thousands of emails following a cyberattack. Also, investors pledged billions for Germany at a major summit in Berlin. DW has more news from Germany.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil's Lula, Flavio Bolsonaro tied ahead of runoff vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb94d0b359f4826344beaec2126dea2c5a16c117bea4ee60ffa1b56de10219c8</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:03:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T15:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brazil-s-lula-flavio-bolsonaro-tied-ahead-of-runoff-vote/a-79715182--cfbbc055c58e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brazil-s-lula-flavio-bolsonaro-tied-ahead-of-runoff-vote/a-79715182?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With just under a week to go before the decisive presidential runoff election, polls show left-wing incumbent Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and his right-wing challenger Flavio Bolsonaro are virtually tied.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Who are the women powering India's youth-led 'Cockroach' protests?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3da31fa191a405f5f6230934cd78205043c28f471a2e26092727c3067316b3d7</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:03:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/who-are-the-women-powering-india-s-youth-led-cockroach-protests/a-79709824--e78a361757e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/who-are-the-women-powering-india-s-youth-led-cockroach-protests/a-79709824?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Facing online harassment and police detentions, women are taking to the streets of Indian cities in large numbers for the youth-led "Cockroach" protests. Amid a large-scale crackdown, they refuse to be seen as victims.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Wagner brothers begin new NBA chapter on different paths</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:80888242ae796f3e10206b69ff8154c4dbcbf171fb5bdd888bc4270d751ca28e</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:02:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wagner-brothers-begin-new-nba-chapter-on-different-paths/a-79712668--ff5544415c4f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wagner-brothers-begin-new-nba-chapter-on-different-paths/a-79712668?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After five years, brothers Franz and Moritz Wagner are no longer playing together for the Orlando Magic. In the new NBA season, their separation will likely mean the new "German" team is the Charlotte Hornets.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Google must have consent to publish property images</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9fe7d4d61874849fdfe83525a1ea835cd1d7497b5718ad9981cad666b7bd0dfa</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:02:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T11:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-google-must-have-consent-to-publish-property-images/a-79712552--7cfbdb603d27.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-google-must-have-consent-to-publish-property-images/a-79712552?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A court in the western German state of Hesse has said Google is "spying" on people and has no right to publish information about their property on its Maps and Earth sites. The case stems from images taken from the air.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Why US investors are snapping up Germany's famed Mittelstand</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:763fc001284c2a46fb2632a50bdfef322e09ea2c38ca834136e00ad70263be68</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:02:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T09:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-us-investors-are-snapping-up-germany-s-famed-mittelstand/a-79705421--453454d6f76c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-us-investors-are-snapping-up-germany-s-famed-mittelstand/a-79705421?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Increasing amounts of US capital are flowing into Germany's traditional industrial firms and family-owned businesses. As many business owners struggle to find successors, more companies are becoming acquisition targets.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Brutal, revolutionary empire builder: Genghis Khan's legacy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:95f8adc784ec9c31fae8a346c5ab4c565696a9449fc7182686b119efd3c44360</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:02:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T08:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brutal-revolutionary-empire-builder-genghis-khan-s-legacy/a-79697112--675146225486.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brutal-revolutionary-empire-builder-genghis-khan-s-legacy/a-79697112?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Berlin is host to a major exhibition on the founder of the Mongol Empire and his successors. Here's how Genghis Khan disrupted the course of history.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Japan probe sets course for Mars moon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:88d1890c533eb387547a16ba869e210e92338041f832957c63d3be240e6cb640</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:02:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T07:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/japan-probe-sets-course-for-mars-moon/a-79708491--8ca3c6616a26.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/japan-probe-sets-course-for-mars-moon/a-79708491?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The MMX spacecraft is on its way to Mars' moon Phobos to collect surface samples that could help answer long-standing questions about the formation of the Solar System.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Rubio holds talks with counterpart Jaishankar</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:241972247ffda2e47d56e7b06a708a009499a03fc8dc19a4a967781119620099</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:02:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T06:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-rubio-holds-talks-with-counterpart-jaishankar/live-79708492--c711a58d8b65.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-rubio-holds-talks-with-counterpart-jaishankar/live-79708492?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Marco Rubio's talks with Indian Foreign Minister Jaishankar come as the two countries struggle to finalize a trade deal.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Canada: Alberta rejects separation bid, CBC projects</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ebe4105b8272d819bded05f5d79d70c0cd89e1e43df61c46e6f3538b4e0a9bf0</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:02:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T06:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canada-alberta-rejects-separation-bid-cbc-projects/a-79708520--59931f2b4e41.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canada-alberta-rejects-separation-bid-cbc-projects/a-79708520?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Voters have decisively rejected a proposal to begin the legal process toward Alberta's independence, dealing a major blow to a movement driven largely by economic grievances.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Australian MP seriously hurt in suspected car attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:615c24a3e5a6670b61922209687816dd9ce21511b136d09270c9bcc0cb9542ed</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:02:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T06:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/australian-mp-seriously-hurt-in-suspected-car-attack/a-79697660--8ec3224c2b82.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/australian-mp-seriously-hurt-in-suspected-car-attack/a-79697660?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Helen Haines, an independent federal lawmaker, suffered severe injuries in what Australia's prime minister has called a deliberate attack by a man in a car.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Christiane Amanpour to leave CNN after 43 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:940542b6fc70d5d962277ad05f9073c12022504a42e2748bbb14f58231cf5b78</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:02:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T03:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/christiane-amanpour-to-leave-cnn-after-43-years/a-79708034--d72b300418b2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/christiane-amanpour-to-leave-cnn-after-43-years/a-79708034?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Christiane Amanpour's announcement comes after Paramount Skydance's controversial merger with Warner Bros. Discovery, CNN's parent company.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Zelenskyy accuses US of delaying Patriot missile shipment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5e9692b35d63b70a39e494fce3a187ce7447187d225eda40064b1a4dd8c47f7</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:02:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T02:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/zelenskyy-accuses-us-of-delaying-patriot-missile-shipment/a-79707951--89d78b10e7ef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/zelenskyy-accuses-us-of-delaying-patriot-missile-shipment/a-79707951?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy has accused the United States of delaying deliveries of air defense missiles already paid for by European allies, as relations between Washington and Kyiv deteriorate.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>At least four dead after flooding in eastern Spain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a6dd0e9c19ef5bc741e420b833436cae1ea2bafba0a0e8c717794abc3aeb50c</id><updated>2026-10-20T20:02:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T00:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/at-least-four-dead-after-flooding-in-eastern-spain/a-79707781--614c93a32fdc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/at-least-four-dead-after-flooding-in-eastern-spain/a-79707781?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At least four people have died in Spain as torrential rain has battered the country's eastern Mediterranean coast. The severe flooding had left more than 450 people stranded on rooftops, in buildings or in cars.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
